 "approvalMessage": {
  "approvalNumber": 48,
  "billId": {
   "basePrintNo": "S52",
   "basePrintNoStr": "S52-2025",
   "printNo": "S52",
   "session": 2025,
   "version": ""
  },
  "chapter": 667,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 48 Chapter 667\n \n         MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 52, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the use of\n        an electronic signature by a person granted a power of  attorney\n        by  a  taxpayer  with  respect to documents submitted to the New\n        York state department of taxation and finance and the  New  York\n        city department of finance\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would amend the tax law to permit individuals with a power\nof attorney to use electronic signatures on any documents  submitted  to\nthe  Department  of  Taxation  and Finance (\"Tax Department\") or the New\nYork City Department of Finance.\n \n  Electronic signatures provide a practical mechanism for efficient  and\naccessible  document  execution. However, this bill would expose the Tax\nDepartment to unwarranted liability while  removing  the  Commissioner's\ndiscretion  to  manage  operational risks effectively. Further, it would\neliminate established compliance procedures, create accountability  gaps\nand  expose  the  State  to  unnecessary legal and financial risk at the\ntaxpayer expense. Therefore, this bill required a chapter  amendment  to\nfix  these issues allowing the Tax Department the opportunity to develop\nan appropriate electronic signature solution that will  enhance  govern-\nment efficiency.\n \n  The  Legislature  has  agreed to this chapter amendment and with these\nchanges, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
